The 28-year-old was found dead in San Francisco shopping mall
A 28-year-old chef who has recently moved to San Francisco has been found dead in stalking a local shopping mall this week.
However, the victim’s fratern says that he can’t arouse someone who would want him to hurt him, noting: “Finally, he was doing business.”
A body found at Westfield Moll on Wednesday Morning was identified as a 28-year-old resident of San Francisco Frank Galicia,” San Francisco for Forensic Examination Bureau said.
The San Francisco Police Department reports that death has been categorized as a homicide and an investigation is ongoing.
The victim’s grater, Luis Galicia, told ABC’ San Francisco-based TV and radio news channel that Frank, the last director of the distribution line in Boston, got his dream job as a chef at San Francisco’s Sons & Daughters restaurant six months ago.
A spokesman for Sons & Daughters said they were “shocked and overwhelmed” by his death.
“We are a small team that works as a close-knit family and will miss it very much,” the representative said.
Our condolences and condolences to Frank's family and friends in this difficult period.
Luis Galicia said that Frank at first stayed in the hostels, but lately "Finally we've been doing business."
“He found the apartment, he was dating a girl,” Luis Galicia told KGO.
Luis Galicia said he couldn’t imagine anyone who wanted to hurt his younger similate.
He had a good soul and a great heart.
His way of connecting with his family has always been to prepare some kind of meurrization to us, prepare us for dinner, ”said Luiz Galicia.
He'd never want to be involved in a quarrel.
He was a brother who floated along the thing.
“With everything bad that is happening with this world, he was that uncut diamond that shone brightly every day,” he said.
Everyone who owns the information is asked to call the SFPD Hotline 415-575-444.
Churkin said that the meeting of the UN Security Council on Crimea was useful.
The permanent representative of the Russian Federation to the UN Vitaly Churkin said that the last meeting of the UN Security Council on Crimea was useful, reports Interfax.
“I think the discussion was useful for us, and we provided them with information about what happened,” Churkin said.
He explained that at the closed consultations of the Security Council, he presented to member states information about the incidents on the territory of the Republic of the Republic of the Crimea and read out a statement of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Russian Federation, which “swebsites concerns and indignation about an attempted terrorist attack and sabotage on the territory of the Republic of the Crimea”.
The men's national team of Russia reached the final of the combined relay race of 4 to 100 m.
The men's team of Russia was able to reach the final of the combined renaissance of 4 to 100 meter in swimming at the Olympiad in Rio de Janeiro.
The Russians in the Qualified presented Anton Chupkov, Evgeny Koptelov, Alexander Sukhorukov and Grigory Tarasevich.
They smeared the distance in 3 minutes 32.95 seconds.
The Russians showed the sixth result.
In the preliminary round the best time for the Britons - 3 minutes 30.47 seconds.
The final will take place late in the evening on Saturday.
Russian rapists defeated the Americans and went to the final of the tournament at the Olympics.
The Russian fencing team reached the final of the team tournament at the Olympic games in Rio de Janeiro.
In the semi-finals, the Russian athletes beat the American national team with a score of 45:41.
The final will take place at 00.30, in it the Russians will have to fight with the team of France, which in the semifinals won a fight with the Italians with a score of 45:30.
The Russian judo operator reached the 1/8 finals of the Olympics
Russian judoquote Renat Said on Friday defeated the Austrian Daniel Allershtorfer in the 1/16 finals of the Olympic games in the category of more than 100 kg, according to the website of the competition.
In the eighth eighth of the final, the Russian will meet with the Brazilian Raphael Silva.
Two of the four gold medals at the Russian Olympiad were brought by judo players.
Beslan Mudranov became the best in the weight category up to 60 kg, Khasan Khalmurzaev - in the category of up to 81 kg.
At the moment the Russian national team occupies the seventh place in the medal standings with 19 awards.
The size of the national debt of Italy has increased to a record
The size of the national debt of Italy in June of 2016 exceeded 2.248 trillion euros.
In the central bank of the country said that this amount is a historical maximum, reports RIA Novosti.
The previous negative record was set in May of this year.
Then the size of the national debt reached 2.228 trillion euros.
It is noted that for the first half of the year the debt load of Italy increased by 77.2 billion euros.
Earlier it was reported that at the end of 2015 the national debt of Italy amounted to 132.7% of the country's GDP.
Meanwhile, the Italian Minister of Economy and Finance Pier Carlo Padoan predicted a decrease in this figure in 2016 to 130.9%, and in 2018 - to 123.4% of GDP.
Payments from the airport received 141 victims of the terrorist attack in “Domodedovo”.
141 people received charitable payouts from the Aviability Fund, which was created by the leadership of Domodedovo airport to help the victims of the terrorist attack in 2011, reports Interfax.
Alexander Vlasov, the press secretary of the airport, now two more applications are under consideration.
“On the part of the fund, charitable payments to victims of the terrorist attack of 2011 are ongoing and comprehensive assistance is provided to resolve existing issues,” Vlasov added, recalling that specifically to facilitate interaction with the victims was a website of the fund containing complete information on the procedure for rendering charitable assistance.
In 2011, a suicide bomber detonated an explosive device in the Arrival of Foreign Airlines.
As a result of the terrorist attack, 37 people were killed, another 172 were injured.
Scientists have found an animal that can live for 500 years
An international group of biologists came to the conclusion that the long-lived vertebruary vertebruary is the Greenland polar shark, which can live for about 500 years.
Scientists conducted a radio-carbon analysis of the crristian of the eye 28 Greenland sharks.
The largest shark, whose length exceeds five meter, can be from 272 to 512 years.
Biologists believe that an important role in longevity of the shark plays a low metabolism, which leads to a slow development.
Female Greenland sharks reach sexual magnificence by the age of 150.
Previously it was believed that the "neighbrower" of the shark - the Greenland whwheat lives for the longest of all vertebruary animals.
The oldest specimen, known to the scientist, was slightly older than the age of 210.
Putin changed the composition of the security Council of the Russian Federation.
The President of Russia Volodymyr Vladimir Putin by his decree made changes to the security Council of the Russian Federation, the press service of the Kremlin reported.
Earlier it became known that Putin withdrew from office the head of the presidential administration Sergei Ivanov, his successor was appointed Anton Vino.
Ivanov will now serve as the special representative of the President on environmental protection, ecology and transport.
From among the permanent members of the Security and Security Council of the Russian feigned the Russian Federation the Deputy Secretary of the Council Rashid Nargaliev.
The Council includes Sergei Ivanov, Anton Vaino, presidential envoy to the SFD Sergey Menyailo and plenipotentiary representative in the SZFoD Nikolai Tsukanov.
Sergei Ivanov was dismissed from the post of the head of the presidential administration.
The decree of the President Sergey Ivanov was relieved from the position of the head of the administration of the Kremlin.
Ivanov was appointed a special representative of the Russian Federation for environmental protection, ecology and transport.
The new head of the administration was appointed Anton Vyno, who previously held the position of Deputy Sergei Ivanov.
According to Vladimir Putin, Ivanov himself asked him to be transferred to another job.
Is it worth going to the sanatorium, if there are no health problems?
Our expert - the chief doctor of sanatorium Olga Bogush.
And if a person is healthy, just tired of work, should he go to a sanatorium?
sanatorium-resort recreation is necessary for us not only for the sake of treatment, but also for the prevention of diseases.
In a sanatorium, a person can check the condition of his body and receive doctor's recommendations on how to live, so that his health does not be destroyed.
Such recommendations will not be uneasable for anyone.
"Just Tired from work" - this is an important signal of the body, you do not have to brush it off.
Continuous stress, mental and physical fatigue can lead to depression and chronic fatigue syndrome.
Approximately 90% of visitors experience stress.
Moreover, people from large cities between the ages of 45 and 55 are most susceptible.
So it is better not to complicate the situation and let yourself rest on time.
Studies show that 98% of people reduce their biological age during their sanatorium while in a sanatorium.
Modern sanatoriums offer a comfortable holiday for the whole family.
Therefore, if you want to spend a vacation with the children, you do not have to break up with them.
For children, even the most young, there are health programs, which include both diagnostic services, pediatric consultations, analyzes, and therapeutic.
For example, swimming (in many sanatoriums there are children's swimming pools), inhalations, a special diet, massages, oxygen cocktails, physical therapy.
The course of procedures is determined by the doctor, taking into account the individual indications and the peculiarities of a growing organism.
In addition, in sanatoriums, as a rule, there is a children's club with animators, where children are able to attend play, various master-characters.
Some sanatoriums open their doors even for guests with infants, provide babysilators with the necessary conditions and provide experienced nanny services.
Soft winter, a long summer, an abundance of sunny days a year (over 300) create good conditions for year-round holidays in the resorts of Caucasian Mineralny Vody.
And then the body needs a holiday not only in the summer.
So you should not be afraid of the weather outside the window, especially since most procedures are carried out in the room and do not depend on the season in any way.
In general, sanatorium-responsive treatment it is advisable to carry out 2 times a year, especially people of adulthood.
The main feature of the Caucasian Mineral Water region, of course, therapeutic mineral springs: Slavyanovsky, Smirnovsky, Essentuki, Narz.
Their waters have unique properties and act on various body systems.
The water differs in temperature, the number of salts, general mineralization, chemical and gas composition.
The doctor selects the water depending on the well-being of the patient.
So, "Narzan" has an anti-inflammatory, immunomodulating effect, restores the functions of the gastrointestinal tract and metabolism.
Essentuki-4 affects the gastrointestinal uterus, reduces the level of sugar.
Essentuki has an anti-inflammatory, choleretic and diuretic effect.
The same problems have water "Slavyanovskaya".
When prescribing water, the doctor necessarily takes into account the state of the cardiovascular system.
If there are signs of hypertension, it collects less saline water, because the sacles retain the liquid, which leads to an increase in pressure.
Receiving the mineral water requires compliance with the regime: the water should be drunk at a certain time, in the right amount and a specific temperature.
Various cosmetologological procedures for the face and body are also available in sanatoriums.
What types of recovery, based on the natural characteristics of the North Caucasus, can be obtained in the resorts of this region?
Near Pyatigorssk, for example, there is a salt lake Tambukan, iliary mud from which is useful for the joints, spine, internal organs.
It exerts an anti-inflammatory, residing, immunomodulatory effect.
These are well-heavalious walks along individually compiled routes.
They are especially popular in Kislovodsk, where there is a huge resort park (the second in size in Europe).
They are popular in Kislovodsk, which is located in close proximity to Narzan mineral source.
There you can also take tunic, pearl baths pearl, iodilous, selenium, sage and lacquers, depending on what the doctor will prescribe to you.
Extend Fructuring.
What can be done so that the harvest goes to the end of the season?
Yulia Belopukova, agronomist and summer cottage.
It's time for high-grown tomatoes to arrange a haircut: to remove new stepsons, cut the mammates, remove all the leaves before the penultimate brush with fruits and inflorescences with small ovaries do not have time to culminate.
All tomatoes, regardless of "constituence", as well as pectores and eggplants are fed with an ash-superfosmatic hood, we are treated with biopreparations (the paternity - to accelerate vilification and growth of fruits, Phytosporin, Phytolavin, Gamair, Bactofit - from diseases, Immunocytophyte - to increase the immune system, Bitoxybacill.
From chemical agents at the end of the summer it should be used only copper sulfur, colloidal sulfur and green soap.
Making the last watering of the plants.
Long-distered cucumbers in the greenhouse are lowered from the speculators so that the lower, bare part of the installement (25-40 cm) lay on the ground, watered with warm water and Zyrkon solution, sprinkle the stalk of 5-7 compost.
It is also not difficult to prolong zucchini fencing: drain the old leaves, spill with warm water and a solution of complex fertilization, spill fertile soil under the bush.
To protect against nocturnal christlies, install an arc with a cover material above the bed.
In the afternoon, keep the plants open, and after sunrise, close.
Features of the end.
What indicates that Russia is emerging from the crisis?
Economists have seen signs of Russia’s withdrawal from the longest recession in the last twenty years.
Analysts interviewed by Bloomberg notes, Russia's GDP demonstrates a positive trend - in the second quarter, GDP decreased by 0.8% in annual terms.
This figure is the lowest since the beginning of 2015.
According to the latest Rosstat data, the decline of the Russian economy in the second quarter slowed to 0.6%.
About the stabilization of the situation, the Central Bank and the Ministry of economic development have also recently said.
Slow growth awaits.
According to CBR experts, the recess in the Russian economy remained in the past.
“The index estimate of Russian GDP suggests that the regression is left behind, and in the ahead – the slow growth of the economy”, – stated in the Bulletin of the Bank of Russia “What the trends are talking about”.
Modular assessment of GDP for the current quarter, the specialists of the regulator increased to 0.4%, the estimate for the fourth quarter is 0.5%.
As reported by the representative of the Ministry of economic development, during the second quarter the decline in the GDP of the Russian Federation stopped in the second quarter, amounting to 0.2%.
In the second quarter, the seasonally refined decline in GDP amounted to 0.2% compared to the previous quarter.
But during the quarter the decline stopped: in April it amounted to 0.2%, and in May and in June the change of GDP was in the range of 0-0.15”, – quotes the representative of the MAYOR RIA “Novosti”.
The slowdown in the fall of the Russian economy during the last five quarters indicates the fact that “the bottom has passed”.
Among the other markers pointing to signs of animated the national economy, Bloomberg calls an increase in demand for electricity and railway transportation, a revitalization of the business.
To make an amendment to the fact that the year leap, it is understandable that the dynamic in plus 1% of electricity consumption can be halved by an additional working day.
We will add a lower average average annual temperature in the first quarter.
The next argument is an increase in freight traffic, but it is difficult to obtain accurate data, and plus or minus 0.5% of the semi-annual volume can also be explained by seasonality, ”explains Kirill Yakovenko from ALOR BROKER.
However, there are other, more obvious signs of stabilizing the Russian economy.
For example, a decrease in price pressure.
In July the consumer price index amounted to 7.2%, compared with 15.6% in the same month last year.
Moreover, for the last two weeks, Rosstat fixes deflation.
Prices in Russia fell for for the first time in five years.
If you look at the dynamics of the ruble, which, albeit showed strong fluctuations at the beginning of the year, according to the end of August since the beginning of the year strengthened by 12%.
This is also one of the signs of a recovery, followed by indicators from the real sector of the economy," Yakovenko said.
In addition, since April in the Russian Federation there has been an increase in the volume of industrial production.
In June the indicator increased by 1.7%.
Slowing the rate of decline in foreign-trade turnover from -32.8% in January of 2016 to -20.7% in May will slow down.
Positive dynamics is also the situation in the labor market, where the level of unemployment decreased to 5.4%.
Behind it was only in September 2015 (5.2%).
Despite the favorable situation in the labor market, the issue with the real disposable income of the population to leave much.
In annual terms, the indicator decreases by 4.8%.
This factor can hinder the recovery of the economy, since household expenditures make a significant contribution to GDP.
As a rule, in the structure of the economy their share exceeds 50%.
In addition to low consumer activity, as risk factors for economic economic growth can also be called a rigid policy of the Bank of Russia.
The regulator keeps the bet of 10.5%, which does not best affect the real sector.
An ungividable factor is an insufficient level of investment, which hinders the development of the industrial potential.
But in general, it can be assumed that by the end of the next of the end of the year the pace of the fall of the Russian economy will slow down to -0.5% against -3.7% in 2015, ”says Irina Rogova, an analyst at Forex Club.
The process of naturalization of the athletes, recently launched in Russian football and has perfectly taken refuge in winter sports at the Olympics in Sochi, is not yet so actively developed in summer sports.
If in the Olympic Games in Rio for Russia and former foreigners, then in most cases we are talking about the origins of the countries - the former republics of the Soviet Union.
But in Rio de Janeiro we can observe the reverse process - a fairly large number of Russians act under the flags of other states.
In each case the history of the change of citizenship is different.
Someone's parents took someone to another country as a child, leaving no choice.
Someone did not withstand the competition for a place as part of the Russian national team.
And someone considered that abroad will create the best conditions for development in the sport.
«AiF.ru” found at least 16 athletes who decided to change their Russian citizenship.
In the German passport of a 27-year-old girl it is written that her name is Lisa Ryzhykh.
Of course, however, she was Elisabeth.
She was born in 1988 in Omsk.
Only four years later, as soon as the Soviet Union collapsed, Lisa’s parents decided to emigrate to Germany.
The girl didn’t have a choice.
There she decided to follow in the footsteps of her older sister - take an athletics around her athletics.
As well as the sister, Lisa chose pole voyages.
It will remain in Russia, it is unlikely to be able to “move from the throne” Elena Isinbayev.
“Unfortunately, at the Olympics in Rio, Lisa will be the only fellow countrywoman, albeit a former, in the pole vaulting sector.
Her the best achievements in this sport - the bronze of the European championship in 2010 and the silver of the continental championship in 2016, which she won again in the absence of Yelena Isinbaeva.
Elena Pirozhkova was born in Novokuznetsk in 1986.
Her parents are religious propagandists of evangelical.
Mostly because of their faith, they left for the United States, when the girl was only three years old.
In addition to Helena, eight more children grew up in the family.
All of them lived in the small town of Grinfield, Massachusetts.
Lena began fond of wrestling at school.
Providing good results, she moved to the city of Koloraado Springs, where in the U.S. Wrestling Training Center continued classes under the leadership of another former Russian Vladislav Izyboynikov.
At the Olympics in 2012 in London, Elena lost in her first fight.
But at the world championship in the same year - a victory.
Before that, by the way, she managed to win silver at the world championship in 2010.
After that there were the bronze of 2013 and the silver of the year 2014.
26-year-old Maria was born in Yaroslavl, where for the first time and got acquainted with a synchronized voyage.
But to say that it was educated by our coaches in Russia, it would be wrong.
Soon the family of the girl decided to emigrate to the United States and settled in the city of Colorado.
That's where Maria continued her studies.
Soon she was already part of the U.S. national team and showed excellent results at the Pan-American Games.
It is understandable that at a serious international level for Russian synchronists it can not compete with competition, but for America its surplosis is a ceiling.
Kristina Shaldybina received a new name in Russian at the age of 11, when her parents made the decision to continue the girl's training of rhythmic gymnastics overseas.
Until this moment, the girl was engaged in the favorite sport in his native Yaroslavl.
Immigrating in the United States, she quickly entered the juniversary team of this country, and later broke into the main national team.
At the Pan-American Gains, 19-year-old Kristen won gold and silver.
For the first positions on the world stage, she, of course, did not need to fight, but for the United States she organized a real breakthrough - brought the star-striped team to the Olympic games in Rio de Janeiro.
Another of our former "artist" - Yana Berezko-Margrander, who plays for the national team of Germany.
Yana was born in Togliatti.
in 2008, when the girl was 13 years old, the family decided to move to Germany - there the girl had more prospects to get to the national team.
Soon she already represented her country at the 2012 Olympic Games in London.
There, however, Yana was able to take only 17 place, not enough to get into the final competition in the personal championship.
But in two years before that, she was able to win the bronze medal of the Olympic Games - the Junior.
Another Gymnastical, only this time sports - Irina Sazonova.
If the emigration of the athletes mentioned earlier can be called standard, the choice of Irina's family is very unusual - Iceland.
Ira is a pupil of the Volgograd sports school.
Of course, in Iceland she immediately became the champion of the country.
However, Ira is still training in Russia - specially come to his homeland, so as not to lose skill.
She didn’t perform as well in Rio as well as she would like.
The best place - 40 in a personal all-around.
There is very little information about the awghander Maria Ugolkova in the Russian information space.
For a very long time, Maria lives and trains in Switzerland.
However, for a long time she performed under the Russian flag, showing good results - there was even a country's record at a distance of 200 meter butterflies.
In 2015, she received Swiss citizenship and began to act under the red-and-and-and-and-white flag.
In Rio, her best performance - 14 place in the complex renaissance of 4 × 100.
To get to the games, the girl launched a crowdfunding project, thanks to which she was able to assemble about 6 thousand francs, which allowed her to pay for preparations for the Olympiad.
31-year-old wrestling wrestler Adam Batirov almost spent his entire career under the Russian flag.
During this time, the native Khasavyurt managed to become a three-time prize-winner of the European championships, the champion of Russia, the master of sports of Russia of international class.
When he ceased to get to our national team, it was time to think about changing citizenship.
For a few years the talented wrestler has disappeared from sports bridges.
Triumphant return took place at the Asian Championship in 2016 - Batirov already represented Bahrain, for whom he won the gold medal and received a ticket to the Olympics in Rio.
About another ex-Rossiyan, Mikhail Kudinov, at the mother-in-law is even less known than even about the Swiss awolf Maria Ugolkov.
The fact is the fact that his parents emigrated from Vladivostok to New Zealand, when the boy was very young.
It’s exactly that Michael began to engage in gymnastics at gymnastics.
He did not achieve great success at the international level.
In Rio, his best result was 40 place in qualifying on parallel bars.
But for New Zealand, even getting to the Olympian games in gymnastics is already a breakthrough.
When Nastya, who was born in Moscow in 1985, was only 9 years old, her family emigrated to Israel.
There the girl continued her synchronized swimming classes, showing high results at the national level.
In 2014, at the European championship in Berlin, the girl took the 6th place in synchronized voyages.
Anastasia ranked eighth in a duet with Yevgeny Tethelbaum eighth.
In the solo program, she was the fifth.
As well as Anastasia, 23-year-old Dmitry Cruyter plays for the national team of Israel.
When the boy was only 6 years of age, his mother decided to repatriate to Israel.
In 2009, at the age of 17, Dmitry has already become the champion of the country.
In the same year, he won the World Junior Youth Championship.
A year later, Croutter also wins the gold of the Youth Olympic Games in Singapore.
In addition to plums in the height, Dmitry is engaged in long-distance jump and a triple jump.
31-year-old Albert - another native of Khasavyurt, who after long performances for Russia decided to change his sports citizenship.
However, in contrast to Batirov, Albert chose Romania, which will be represented in Rio.
In Russia, he competed for Krasnoyarsk’s Higher Athletic School of Higher Athletic Sculpture, in 2011 he even became the champion of the country.
28-year-old Oleg Antonov was born in Moscow in the family of a player of the USSR volleyball Yaroslav Antonov.
Literally a year before the birth of his son, Yaroslav was recognized as the best volleyball player of the planet.
Soon he decided to pursue a career in Italy.
There the same family remained for permanent residency.
In 2015, as part of the national team, he became the Bronze Prize-winner of the European Championship, which was held on the territory of his new homeland.
Khadziev was born in Chechnya in 1994 and got with his family in the midst of the war.
After ten years, the parents decided to emigrate.
The original goal was Norway, but it was not possible to get into this northern country - I had to go to France, to Nice.
There Zelimkhan continued to study freestyle wrestling.
Soon he won the world junior world championship, and later qualified to participate in the Olympic Games.
In Rio, he will be the only representative of France in the wrestling tournament.
And again freestyle wrestling, and again a former Russian.
This time we will talk about a native of North Ossetia, who emigrated to St. Spain - Taymuraz Friev.
At the end of December 2012 he was granted Spanish citizenship, and he is currently competing for the national team of this country.
Before that, however, the 30-year-Leagued athlete managed to score high results in Russia.
He became the Bronze Prize-winner of the championship of the country in 2007 and 2008.
Tired of not falling into the national team, Taimuraz decided to change sports citizenship.
The latter in our list is the Chechen boxer, who was born in 1995 in the capital of Dagestan Makhachkala - Arthur Biyarslanov.
When the child was ten years old, his parents took the family through Azerbaijan to Canada.
There Arthur on the advice of his older brother started boxing.
Since then, Artur has become the champion of Canada three times, and in 2012 became the world champion among young people.
In 2015, Biyarslanov won the gold of the Pan-American Games, the first for his new homeland since 1975.
The head of the administration of the President of the Russian Federation Anton Vino.
On Friday, August 12, Vladimir Putin appointed Anton Vyno the head of the presidential administration of Russia.
Previously this position was held by Sergei Ivanov.
“The head of state by his decree has appointed Anton Vaino the head of the presidential administration of the Russian Federation, releasing him from office”, – stated in the decree signed by Putin and published on the Kremlin’s website.
Since May 2012, Vaino was the Deputy head of the presidential administration of the Russian Federation.
Anton Eduardovich Vaino was born on February 17, 1972 in Tallinn.
The father is Eduard Vyno, the Chairman of the Kuba-Russia Business Council in the Chamber of Commodity and Industry of the Russian Federation and the vice-president for external relations and interaction with the shareholders of AvtoVAZ.
Grandfather - Karl Vyno - from 1978 to 1988 the First Secretary of the Central Committee of the Communist party of Estonia.
In 1996 he graduated from the Moscow State Institute of International Affairs of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Russia, the faculty of international relations.
From 1996 to 2001, he worked in the Russian Embassy in Japan, then in the Second Department of Asia of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Russian foreign Ministry.
From 2002 to 2004 he held various positions in the Office of the Protocol of the President of the Russian Federation.
From 2004 to 2007 - Deputy head of the protocol-organizational department of the President of the Russian Federation.
From 2007 to 2007 - First deputy head of the protocol of the President of the Russian Federation.
From October 2007 to April 2008 - deputy head of the apparatus of the government of the Russian Federation.
April 25, 2008 was appointed the head of the protocol of the Chairman of the Government of the Russian Federation, Deputy Head of the Administrative Department of the Government of the Russian Federation.
Since December 27, 2011 - The Minister of the Russian Federation - the head of the Office of the Government of the Russian Federation.
May 22, 2012 was appointed deputy head of the Presidential Administration of the Russian Federation.
Favour of English and Japanese fluent English.
Current State Adviordinator of the Russian Federation of the 1st class (a class rank was awarded by the Decree of the President of the Russian Federation of January 22, 2008)
Letter of Honor of the President of the Russian Federation (February 16 February 2012) for merits in ensuring the activities of the Government of the Russian Federation and many years of conscientious work.
Gratitude of the President of the Russian Federation (November 24, 2005) for merit in the preparation and holding of ceremonial events commemoration dedicated to the 60th Anniversary of the Victory in the Great Patriotic Patriotic War.
Married, has a son.
Why do children of Cossack classes in schools?
According to Governor V. Kondratyev, “Concise should not be brought up with actions and ceremonial parades, but systematically.”
They need to grow and from at least the age of 7 understand that they are Cossacks and education should be Cossack.
But while this work, it seems to me, is carried out formally and, I suspect, more on paper.
If the Cossack classes conceive of everything that has accumulated earlier, at a qualitatively new level, I will be happy.
If it’s all awk and unambiguous, a new idea will turn into cheap populism.
utilities continues to be one of the most criminal sectors of the country's economy.
Encroachments have taken place on the funds allocated for the utilities from the budgets of different levels.
According to the Prosecutor General’s office, overpriced tariffs are one of the most common crimes in the housing and communal utilities.
As a result, the consumers of the region overpaid more than 170 million rubles to power engineers.
On the other day, the Prosecutor’s office of the Krasnodar region revealed the facts of the inclusion of unreasonable costs in tariffs.
And 4 million rubles were pledged in the expenses of LLC "IV-Consulting" (substituted cold water) on the rental of cars at a price higher than the market.
And there are a lot of such examples in the country.
The people donates the last money for communal money, and pays properly - according to the Ministry of Construction of the Russian Federation, the average collection of payments from the population is 94%.
He is accused under several articles of the criminal code: embezzlement, the legalization of proceeds of criminal proceeds, an abuse of authority, etc.
According to the investigation, as the head of the fund, which was engaged in the repair of urban facilities, Makarov entered into contracts with entrepreneurs, the work on them was actually not carried out, but were paid.
Businessmen just returned him most of the money.
And as the owner of the criminal code, Makarov collected money from the population, but the service providers did not pay and spent them on their own needs.
AS a result, the damage to the budget and the tenants - millions of rubles.
Scheme of Makarov machinations, awurn, is typical for Russia.
In the country there was a whole wave of arrests and detains of the leaders of the criminal code, which appropriated the money of the citizens.
In Kamchatka continues the trial of A. Kohan, by the way, a former deputy of the city Council, who is accused of fraud for 91.7 million rubles.
