The Portuguese air force said today that the P-3C Orion pilot performed a training flight to detect fishing boats off the coast, and was forced to drop so low, since it was the only way to test them.
Pilot said that the aircraft flew a little lower than usual due to insufficient visibility caused by the smoke from nearby burning forests, but the air force insisted that no one was at risk.
This summer, forest fires caused damage to the mainland of Portugal, as well as claimed the lives of four people on the island of Madeira.
