HUSSP system for more than a year is obligatory for catering, but most cafes and restaurants in St. Petersburg have not yet been implemented.
Checks are becoming more active, and the business faces fines of up to 1 million rubles.
For more than a year the Hazard Analysis and Critical Control Points (HACCP, in the Russian version of HACCP) - analysis of risks and critical checkpoints - is required to use food manufacturers and carriers, as well as companies in the field of catering in Russia, as a member of the Customs Union (TS).
Business checks by Rospotrebnadzor for compliance with these norms in St. Petersburg began in February 2015.
But for so far, officials are issuing fines only for certain violations of the regulation (see "List of documents" ...).
Failure to comply with the regulations as a whole will cost the enterprise 600 thousand rubles for the first violation and in 1 million rubles for the second.
KhACSP as a system, taking into account the risks when working with food and preventing them, was invented in the United States in the 1960-ies.
At the same time it was about the safety of meals for astronauts.
Now the system is used in all food enterprises not only in the United States, but also in Canada and in the European Union.
Since February 2015, KhACSP has been operating on the territory of the Customs Union.
On the development and implementation of the business system was 4 years old (KHASP requirement appeared in the technical regulation of the CU in 2011).
However, both entrepreneurs themselves and officials admit that most companies did not even hear about this norm.
We, unfortunately, for a long time were sure that the norm applies only to food industries, not restaurateurs, ”explained Elena Tsereteli, head of the Public Council.
Now everyone's trying to catch up.
Expediable period for the resumption of charter flights to Turkey - the end of August - the beginning of September.
But they won’t cause a fusing demand, since their target audience—families with children—is already being prepared for school, experts say.
The Alliance of Travel Agencies yesterday sent a letter to the government with a request now to resolve charters.
“For many Russian tourists, the issue of the selection of high-quality and affordable maritime recreation is unresolvable, because in the resorts of the Krasnodar Territory and the Republic of the Republic of Crimea, most accommodation facilities have already been booked by the end of September,” the authors of the letter note and emphasize that the opening of charter flights in August will not significantly affect the already existing demand for the Russian marine tourist.
As reported in the North-Western regional branch of the Russian Union of tourism industry, in the event that the aviation ministries of Russia and Turkey quickly agree, the resumption of charter flights to Turkey can be expected within a month.
There is no clear comprehensibility, when the charters will be resumed, it depends primarily on the aeronautical authorities.
Airplanes can technically fly in September, even in August, if the tour operators promptly build programs and make an agreement with airlines on the sides needed on the direction, ”said Pavel Rumyantsev, deputy director for communications and international projects of the North-Western regional branch of PCT.
According to him, the possible resumption of charters is good news, but it will not affect the alignment of forces in the market too much, because the main buyers of charter tours - families with children - have already returned from vacation and are preparing for the school or spend their holidays in other countries.
In the velvet season, tours are bought mainly by solitary travelers and pairs.
Charter programs can count on those who have the opportunity to rest spontaneously, ”says Pavel Rumyantsev.
“Turkish has a chance of attracting a lot of tourists, if it now gives a lot of budget offers – 50-60 thousand rubles per tour for two, because there are people who are purposefully waiting for very cheap tours,” says Valeria Rosenthal, general director of Optio-Travel travel agency.
In other cases, it is definitely not worth counting on the excitement - the main mass of travel has already been planned.
Pavel Rumyantsev also believes that, since there is a demand for regular flights to Turkey, charters will also be in demand, but you do not expect hype.
“For Turkey, the launch of charters now is a rehearsal next season,” says Pavel Rumyantsev.
“Discovery of charters in Turkey - positive news for the next season," Valeria Rubtsov agrees.
The tax code provides for the exemption from personal personal income of personal personal personal income of compensatory payments within the limits of the approved norms associated with compensation for the harm caused by mutilation or other undiviance of health.
Issuance to employees engaged in work with bad working conditions of milk according to established standards is provided for by article 222 LC of the Russian Federation.
At the Same time, the norms and conditions of issuance themselves are established by an order of the Ministry of Health and Social Development of the Russian Federation dated 16.02.2009 No.
According to this document, the free issuance of milk or other equivalent food products is carried out to workers on the days of actual employment in works with harmful working conditions, due to the presence of harmful production factors in the workplace due to the presence of harmful production factors in the workplace.
Proceeding from these norms, the Federal Tax Service of the Russian Federation in this letter came to the conclusion that, on the basis of paragraph 3 of article 217 of article 217 of the Criminal Code of the Russian Academy of Commodity Flee, income in the form of the cost of milk donated to employees in the days of actual employment in works with harmful working conditions in accordance with the Norms and conditions approved by the order of the Ministry of Health and Social Development of the Russian Federation of 16.02.
Moskovsky “Gazstroybank” was left without a license of the Central Bank.
On Friday, August 12, 2016, the Central Bank of Russia revoked a license to carry out banking operations from a credit institution Joint-stock Commercial Bank GAZSTRAYBANK, which is registered in Moscow.
According to the Regulator, GAZSTROYBANK JSC conducted a high-pricted credit policy associated with the placement of funds in low-quality assets.
An adequate assessment of risks taken at the request of the supervisory authority and a reliable reflection of the value of the bank's assets led to the emergence by the credit institution of grounds for the implementation of measures to prevent bankruptcy.
In addition, the credit institution was engaged in dubious transit operations.
In the bank, a temporary administration has been appointed a period of expiration before being appointed to a competitive manager or a liquidator.
Executions of executive bodies of the credit institution in accordance with federal laws are suspended.
GAZSTRAYBANK JSC is a member of the deposit insurance system.
It will be reminded that the payment of insurance indemnity compensation to depositors of the bank, including individual entrepreneurs, in accordance with the Federal Law No. 177-FZ "On Insurance of Deposits of Individuals in the Banks of the Russian Federation" is provided in the amount of a 100% balance of funds, but not more than 1.4 million ruble in aggregate per depositor.
Payments, according to the Deposit Inaslement Insurance Agency, will begin no later on August 26, 2016
According to the reporting data, GAZSTROYBANK on August 1, 2016 accounted for 335 place in the banking system of the RUSSIAN banking system on August 1, 2016.
