FAS will be penalized by Google for 438 million rubles.
The Federal Antimonopoly service of Russia (FAS) has imposed an administrative fine against Google in the amount of 438 million rubles, according to the agency’s website.
“Finnish for Google for violating antimonopoly legislation amounted to 438 million rubles.
We hope that the company will fulfill our decision and will pay a fine in the near future”, – said the Deputy head of the FAS Aleksey Dotsenko.
In the course of an investigation, the FAS found that Google supplies smartphone makers, which are sold in the territory of Russia, the Google Play app store only on condition that other applications of the corporation will be installed on the device.
Among these applications there is also a search engine, which should be placed on the main screen of a smartphone.
Thus, the corporation violates Part 1 of Art. 10 of the Federal Law "On the protection of competition" (abuse of a dominant position).
We are confident that the fulfillment of the prescription will provide an opportunity to develop competition in the market of mobile software in Russia, which will positively affect our consumers.
The law “Protecting competition” must be observed by all companies whose products are supplied to the territory of the Russian Federation and to transnational corporations, among other things, ”said Elena Zaeva, Head of the Communications and Information Technologies Regulatory Regulatory Department of the FAS of Russia.
