The government has promulgated the expiration of sanctions products
Until the end of 2017, the government has extended until the end of 2017, the period for the destruction of foodstuffs prohibited for import into Russia.
The corresponding resolution was signed by the Prime Minister Dmitry Medvedev, it is published on the official portal of legal information.
Embrango in relation to countries that introduced anti-Russian sanctions due to the situation in Ukraine, was introduced in our country in August 2014.
Subsequent, the ban was repeatedly extended, now it is valid until December 31, 2017.
It is forbidden to import certain types of agricultural products, raw materials and food from the United States, the countries of the European Union, Canada, Australia, Norway, Ukraine, Albania, Montenegro, Iceland and Lichtenstein.
In particular, meat and meat products, fish, seafood, vegetables, fruits and dairy products were banned.
Recycling of food, imported in the country bypassing the embargo, has been carried out in Russia since August 2015.
Only in the first quarter of 2016 about 100 tons of prohibited products were withdrawn from sale.
"Prohibition Hunting"
Rains and thunderstorms are expected in Moscow on Friday.
Through the metropolitan region there will be an atmospheric front, which will bring precipitation and reduce the air temperature.
In the afternoon the air will warm up to 25 degrees Celsius.
So, on the night of Saturday in some places there will be a short-term dreary rain, thunderstorms and gusts of the wind of up to 15 m / s are possible.
In the afternoon, rain is expected with thunderstorms and ghosts of the wind up to 12-17 m / s.
Rains with thunderstorms are also predicted in the Orel, Kursk and Voronezh regions, according to “Dash.ru”.
Precipitation in the next working week is uncommencing.
The panel of arbitrators of the WTO found that Russian import duties on paper, refrigerators and palm oil are contrary to the rules of the organization.
Introductory bets exceed the obligations assumed by Russia when joining the WTO.
“This is the first case when the WTO made a decision against the Russian Federation”, – said in a statement on the organization’s official website.
The arbitrators, however, stressed in their opinion that the European Union did not provide sufficient evidence that Russia’s measures were “complicated.”
Russia, in turn, promised in the near future to adapt import duties on paper and flat-reflectors in the near future.
This is stated in the message of the Ministry of economic development of Russia.
On July 4, it was reported that Kiev intends to complain to the World Trade Organization about the actions of Russia, which has imposed additional restrictions on the transit of Ukrainian goods.
This is stated in the statement of the government of Ukraine.
In May, the Financial Times wrote that the behavior of the United States when solving controversial issues in the WTO undermines the principles of the discussions adopted in the organization.
Such a statement was made by Brasilia, Japan, the European Union and other WTO members due to the refusal of the Americans to approve for a second term of the South Korean judge Jang Sung-hwa.
In this regard, Russia will not apply to the WTO on the issue of Western sanctions imposed against the Russian Federation.
The WTO is an international organization established in January 1995 to liberalize international traversy.
Now it consists of 162 countries.
Russia Joined it in 2012.
