The United Nations is investigating the use of chemical weapons in Syria.
The UN special commission is investigating the possible use of toxic gas in rebel-held areas of Aleppo.
All the parties to the conflict denies the use of chlorine, but UN special envoy for Syria Steffan de Mistura considers the fact of what happened undeniable.
Such statements were made on the basis of the third round of intra-Syrian negotiations, which should begin at the end of August in Geneva.
UN experts began an investigation into reports about the use of chemical weapons in the Syrian city of Aleppo.
The first information about the terrorist attack with the use of toxic gas, presumably chlorine, appeared on August 2.
Then the opposition said that in the area where a Russian military transport helicopter was shot down the day before, the aircraft dropped bombs with a poisonous substance, but in Moscow these accusations were called stuffing.
Later the Ministry of defense of the Russian Federation blamed what was the incident the opposition group “Kharakat Nur al-Din al-Zinki”.
Soon it became known that there were two bombs filled with toxic gas.
This was confirmed to the BBC by one of the victims.
“A few minutes a few minutes later I felt the smell of the gas, began to burn the eyes, it became difficult to breathe,” the eyewit person said.
As a result of the attack, at least 7 people were killed, 23 were hospitalized.
If the fact of the use of toxic gas is confirmed by the experts, the actions will be regarded as a war crime.
UN Special Envoy for Syria, Staffan de Mistura, told reporters: “There’s a lot of evidence that this has indeed happened.”
Abnorbitant use of chlorine for military purposes is spelled out in the Convention on the Prohibition of Chemical Weapons (CHO).
Despite the fact that all the parties to the Syrian conflict denies the use of toxic gases, in 2015 human rights activists recorded 35 cases of chlorine use by the Syrian army against “moderate opposition”.
The situation in Aleppo complicates the fact that the shelling of its areas is carried out on a daily basis, and the terrorists are presupposed to remove residents from the city.
As reported by Reuters, the UN is expecting from Russia to establish a “humanitarian pause” in military operations.
The current regime of a daily three-hour lull in the organization considers “insufficient to help the almost 2 million civilians trapped”.
Staffan de Mishura’s humanitarian adviser Jan Eguelann said that a 48-hour cease-createllance would be required to deliver aid and evacuate the sick and wounded to the city.
“We have to send voluminous loads with a convoy of trucks in an area where the roads are almost destroyed, and those who remained are mined”, – said Mr. Egelann. – But the Russian delegation confirmed its readiness to sit with us at the negotiating negotiating table.
Consultations in Geneva between representatives of the United States and Russia regarding the establishment of a “humanitarian pause” are ongoing.
how Russia opened “Humanitarian windows” in Aleppo
In the context of the ongoing battle for Aleppo - the second-largest Syrian city - Russia on August 11 announced the imposition of a three-hour cessation of hostilities, which will be valid every day from Thursday.
Creating “Humanitarian windows” is intended to provide conditions for the delivery of medicines, food and basic necessities to the city.
The decision of the Ministry of defense of the Russian Federation was made against the backdrop of intensifying international pressure on Moscow with a demand to curtail a military operation and contribute to the resumption of the negotiation process.
As a result of a series of explosions in the resort of Thailand, four people were killed.
At once several explosions thundered in the south of Thailand on Friday in the morning.
As a result of the attack, four people were killed, 19 were wounded.
The epicenter of the blast fell on the city of Hua-Hin.
Among the victims there were ten foreigners, citizens of four states, there are no Russians among them.
Any of the terrorist groups has not yet taken responsibility for the incident, but the interior of the country hurried to declare that the Islamists are not involved in it.
On suspicion of organizing the bangs, several people have already been detained.
According to preliminary data of the local police, the scale and peculiarities of the explosions indicate that they were directed against heads of the military.
Attacks took place at popular tourist resorts, including Pathong beach near Phuketa and Hua Khin, Trang and Surat Thani.
After the military junta coming to power in 2014, economic growth fell from 7.2% (2012) to 2.8% (2015), but tourism remained one of the few industries that demonstrated development.
In 2016, the country was already visited by 14 million people, which is 1.5 million more than in 2015.
Already detained the first suspects in the preparation and organization of the attacks, said police colonel Khrizana Patanacharoen.
While it is too early to talk about goals, he added, but in the interior Ministry of the country "we are sure that they are not associated with international extremist groups."
It's too early to draw conclusions, - said Mr. Patanacharoen.
But we know for sure that these incidents are not directly related to any type of terrorism, in fact it is local sabotage, and we are trying to establish the facilitation of those who stood behind.
Explosions took place on the birthday of the Queen of Thailand Sycrit.
The Thai junta considers the protection of the monarchy to be one of its main priorities, so the incident, most likely, is directed against it.
According to the statements of the police General Sithic Srisopacharoenarate, the bombs were detonated with a difference of half an o'clock.
They were hid inside the trees on busy streets, filled with tourists dining in restaurants.
It is already well known that one of the four of the dead was a Thai girl selling street food.
The identities of the rest of the victims are still unknown, but it is known that they are residents of four foreign countries.
According to the royal police of Thailand, among them four German citizens, three subjects of the Netherlands, two Italian citizens and a citizen of Austria.
There are no Russians among the victims of the explosions, said the press service of Rostourism.
Local experts also associate the blamshells with the referendum held on August 7, in which 61.4% of the country's population supported the draft of the new constitution.
It was prepared by a commission for the drafting of the constitution, appointed by the military junta.
Voters had to decide whether they supported a system in which the upper house of parliament is fully appointed by the military and has a significant role in the election of the country's prime minister.
The new system was adopted and for the first time will be tested in the parliamentary elections of 2017.
We will remind, on May 22, 2014, a military coup took place in Thailand under the leadership of the commander of the army of the country Prayuth Chang-Ocha.
To this step, according to him, the army was inspired by the ongoing political crisis and the lack of progress in the negotiations between the government and the opposition.
The military created the National Council for peace and order, imposed curfews and censorship, dismantivated the protesters and the upper house of parliament.
how Bangkok was in a state of emergency
The government of Thailand, headed by Prime Minister Yjinglak Shinawatra in January 2014, declared a state of emergency in Bangkok and adjacent to the provincial capital.
The special regime lasted for 60 days.
There were two bangs in Bangkok.
In January 2014, in the center of Bangkok near the Victory Monument, where one of the main protests took place, there were two explosions, as a result of which 28 people were injured, five of them were in critical condition.
Explosions were carried out by unscrupulants on motorcycles.
The authorities strengthened security measures in the capital and attracted military forces to protect demonstrators.
In the Sukhoi Loga began the development of conditions.
As it became known to Kommersant, the government is invited to agree on a draft of the auction on the Sukhoi Log gold ore deposit with the preservation of two key restrictions.
It is proposed not to admit the auction to a company, where 25% more belongs to foreigners, and those applicants whose capital there will not be at least 25% of state-of-participation.
Industry participants do not expect that the government will rewrite conditions, noting that many players already do not at the risk of embarking on a complex and expensive project.
Auction can be announced in August, and held - in October.
The Ministry of Natural Resources has submitted to the government a draft order and auction conditions for the largest undeveloped non-developed gold ore deposit in Russia Sukha Log (Irkutsk region, reserves and resources - 130 million ounces), two Kommersant sources familiar with the situation said.
The project was introduced on Wednesday evening, one of them clarifies.
Kommersant of the Ministry of Natural Resources confirmed that the project was submitted to the government.
The representative of Deputy Prime Minister Alexander Khloponin, who oversees subsoil use, told Kommersant that the project has not yet been submitted to the official’s office.
“The auction can be announced already in August, immediately after the issuance of the order of the government, and taking into account the period for the collection of applications of potential participants (not less than 45 days), the tender may take place in October”, – said the Ministry of natural resources.
According to Kommersant, two key requirements for potential participants have been retained, spelled out in the version, which was sent for approval to the Ministries and FOIV in Juniors (Kommersant has it).
The first - the presence in the capital of applicants of at least 25% of state participation.
The second is the denial of access to the auquet for companies under the control of foreign investors, based on an understanding of FZ-57 about foreign investments in strategic societies.
Pursuant to the two articles of the Federal Law specified in the draft, as Kommersant already wrote on August 2, companies whose beneficiaries (25% and above) do not include tax residencies of the Russian Federation or have dual citizenship may prevent the auction.
The government has the right to impose such restrictions, since Dry Log refers to the subsoil of federal importance (reservations of more than 50 tons of gold).
In the Ministry of natural resources confirmed that the project “contains restrictions on the admission of foreign companies”, but refused to comment on the details before the order of the government.
The demand for state participation in the capital of the auction participants was put forward by the Irkutsk region, Kommersant was said in December 2015 to the Ministry of Natural Resources and was later confirmed by the governor of the region Sergey Levchenko, noting that it was sent to the Ministry of Natural Resources by his predecessor Sergei Eroshchenko, who "haved an agreement on investment projects with Rostec."
Who lobbied the restriction on the admission of foreigners, the interlocutors of Kommersant do not specify.
“But this is in the spirit of the time: do not give control in the largest field of gold in Russia against the background of Western sanctions”, – says the interlocutor of Kommersant, who is familiar with the preparation of the auction.
The President of the Ministry of natural Affairs Sergey Donskoy on August 1 stated that foreigners “can go to a consort”, if the applicants involve them “as a financial structure, technological partners”.
Interlocutors of “Kommersant” consider it unlikely that the government will adjust conditions.
The main contender for Sukha Log in the industry is the consortium of the largest gold miner of the Russian Federation PJSC "Polyus", controlled by the son of Suleiman Kerimov Said and "Rostec".
As "Kommersant" wrote, in July, the partners created the SP "SL Gold", where "Polyus" has a 51% stake, Rostec RT - 49%.
Rostec refused to commentally, Polyus told Kommersant that “certificately they are interested in this asset and have all the necessary competencies and resources for its development.
“But the final decision on the possibility and format of our participation will be made after declaring conditions”, – said in the “Polyus”.
ALROSA can participate in the auction, but the decision is for the government of the Russian Federation, Kommersant sources said.
About the possibility of participation in the development of Sukhoi Log said the Russian GV Gold and the Canadian Kinross, which develops assets in Chukotka, while Polymetal and Nordgold, according to Kommersant, are not interested in an asset.
The head of the Union of gold miners of the Russian Federation Sergey Kashuba in December 2015 evaluated “Kommersant” investments in Sukhoi Log at $ 2.5-4 billion.
The majority of potential claimants are scared not only from the volume of investments, but also the complexity of the project: we need a serious reconnaissance of supplies and technologies of working with complex ores, Kommersant interlocutors in the industry explain.
In the pension market started the largest M&A transaction - "KIT Finance Pension Administrator" launched the process of uniting the four controlled NPFs.
As a result on the basis of "Gazfond Pension Savings", NPF will be created with an amount of savings about 373 billion rubles.
About the start of the procedure for the unification of the four pension funds - "KIT Finance", "Promagrofond", "Healing" and "Gazfond Retired Savings" said yesterday the owner of 100% of the funds LLC "KIT Finance Pension Administrator".
“The reorganization is carried out in coordination with the Central Bank in compliance with the requirement of unwhelming the conditions of existing contracts”, – stated in the message of the company.
Unification is carried out on the basis "Gazfond Pension Savings".
As the general director of this NPF, Oleg Bayloshitsky notes, the unification of the funds allows to solve several tasks: expanding the geography of the presence, consimplification of resources for the development, reducing costs, replicating the best practices of each of the funds and optimizing corporate governance.
According to him, the approximative deadline for the completion of the constituency is the second quarter of 2017.
AS a result of the merger NPF "Gazfond Pension Accumulators" will become the largest player in the OPS market.
According to March 31, the volume of retiring savings of unsuitable funds exceeded 373 billion rubles.
As it follows from the statements on the website of the funds, the beneficiaries of their owner - "KIT Finance Retiring Administrator" - are currently Anatoly Gavrilenko (through controlled LLC owns 65%) and NPF "Gazfond" (35%).
However, the unification of the group itself launched a lot later than the competitors.
So, controlled by NPF NPF “Busday” cognated “Stalfond” at the beginning of this year.
At the present time, this united NPF is joining Uralsib and Russian Standard funds.
“Unification into a single structure, in addition to reducing costs, it is necessary to solve structural problems”, – said Nikolay Sidorov, General Director of NPF “Future”.
An active work on the consolidation of the funds since April is also going on in the pension group "Safmar" - NPF "Europe", "Education and science" and "Regionfond" should be joined by NPF "Safmar" until the end of this year.
In 2017, they will be joined by NPF "Confidence".
“Unification of funds will give the effect of increasing control of risks, operating processes and expenses”, – noted the pension group “Safmar”.
A pause in the unification of the funds, which was withstand "KIT Finance Retired administrator", can be caused by a few reasons, experts say.
Until recently, NPF could not repurchase more than 40% of the volume of issue of infrastructural bonds, in which the group was actively positioned.
After making amendments to the Central Bank's resolution in March of this year for a number of issueplants that complied with the requirements of the Regulator, there are no such restrictions anymore.
If you need the entire issue can be repurchased by one major player, ”said Yuri Nogin, director of a group of financial ratings of ACRA financial institutions.
Several NPF executives from the top -15 in terms of the assets of another possible pause call the division of spheres of influence and, as a result, personnel appointments in a single fund, which the owners of the group were to be agreed upon.
Anatoly Gavrilenko was unavailable for comment.
At the request of "Kommersant" in NPF "Gazfond" also did not respond.
Although the consolidation of the funds is a labor-intensive and undesirable event, at a long distance this decision will be justified.
As the General Director of the consulting company "Pension Partner" Sergey Okolesnov, "Gazfond Pension Savings" has fewer outflows, joining will allow to stabilize the basis of other funds of the group.
At the same time, a more successful experience of NPF "KIT Finance" and "Promagrofond" will be in demand in the construction of retail sales OPS, as well as the use of a more modern software.
The requirements of the Central Bank for the processes and personnel of NPF are constantly growing, so it is impractical to duplicate the infrastructure on four funds with a single investment policy, says Pavel Mitrofanov, managing director for corporate ratings of Expert RA.
“The effect from reducing duplicate functions will unequivocally block the possible costs of unification”, – said Mr. Mitrofanov.
Expenditures for the unification of the four funds Sergey Okolesnov estimates at 30-50 million rubles.
Expenditures for the maintenance of four funds of these sizes are about 400 million rubles a year, with the consolidation in the medium term, the budget is really reduced by halving," Mr. Okolesnov said.
In the Russian box office there was a kind of Disney movie “Pete and his dragon”.
The beautiful views of New Zealand, a saturated dragon, soulful history and country-style songs are enough to again believe old-fashioned magic, says ELENA KRAVTSUN.
Frightened baby was picked up a dragon, which became the human cub and a delicate babysitter, and a devoted friend.
