The Spiritual Directorate of Muslims (DUM) of Tatarstan renounces the use of the Russian language in mosques.
Yesterday, printus DOOM obliged its imams to conduct Friday sermons only in Tatar, in order to force young Tatars to “study their native language”.
In the office say that this “in any case does not impracticate” the rights of Muslims of other nationalities.
In some mosques, Kazan complain that the Tatar language does not understand up to 60% of parishioners, among whom are foreign students, migrants and Tatars themselves.
The imams fear that their servages in Tatar "will not reach the whole audience."
Yesterday, plem
Kamil Samigullin told the mufti of Tatarstan, this should be a stimulus for young Tatars to “study their native language”.
“For those who will say that “heaviness”, in every large mosque we intend to organize the lessons of the Tatar language absolutely for free,” Mr. Samigullin said.
He added that "the decision has already entered into force" and today in all mosques of sermons "should be already in the Tatar language."
He reminded that DOUM of Tatarstan publishes the magazine "Shura" with standard sermons in the Tatar language.
An imam who doesn't speak Tatar well enough "may be thoroughly prepared for them."
DOUM of Tatarstan unites more than a thousand parishes in all municipalities of the republic.
According to the mufti, Friday's sermons are conducted exclusively in Tatar ones.
At the same time in Kazan in a number of Mosques previously used predominantly the Russian language.
In particular, according to the mufti, this was practiced in the Burnaev Mosque, Zakabannaya and Enyler.
However, Mr. Mukhametzyn stressed, the management sets the task that all students speak both state languages of the republic, regardless of their nationality.
“There is no question of any infringement of non-nattar Muslims,” Mr. Mukhametshin stressed, explaining that the sermon itself “is not an obligatory, the main part of the pharmacy”.
At the same time the prayer itself will continue to be repainted in Arabic, lectures and Russian lessons will be preserved in mosques.
At the same time, Rafik Mukhametshin told Kommersant that there was no serious threat of ousting the Tatar language from mosques.
In addition to Russian and Tatar other languages, such as Uzbek or Tajik, according to him, are not used in sermons in the republic.
The decision of DUM was actively supported in the executive committee of the World Tatar Congress (WC).
Rinat Zakirov, the head of VKT Executive Committee told Kommersant: “Mosches are an important part of our national life.”
It would be a shame if the Tatar language left this sphere.
He noted that conducting sermons only in the Tatar language "the desire of the imams themselves", but the CTB Executive Committee "consider it right."
Retrieved “Kommersant” imams who preached in Russian, are ready to fulfill the decision of the Duma, but they believe that the parishioners will have difficulties with an understanding of the clergy.
In the mosque there are both Tatars and the Russians.
Many don't understand the language.
Of course they will be obscure.
“You will have to be rebuilt”, – says imam of the Burnaev Mosque Farkhat Maveltdinov.
According to him, sermons in the Russian language are closer even to many Tatars, since "the Russians both in schools and in children's gardens, on the radio - everywhere initially."
However, he believes that in the mosque they will be able to continue lessons and Lectures in Russian, which are held on other days.
We relied on God.
“Ablohammall comes a way out of this situation,” he concluded.
But about 60% we don't know Tatarian.
These are Uzbeks and Tajiks, and Azerbaijanis.
There are a lot of foreign students come to us: the Africans, the Arabs.
“Therefore, for four years we have switched to the Russian language”, – ssays the imam.
He believes that sermon in the Tatar language will “recommended to a narrower circle and will not reach the entire audience.”
But we're going according to the pleuntan solution.
It's just that the servants will be different.
But the time will tell.
“I, for example, it will only be easier for me, because the Tatar language is my native language,” Gabdullah Galiullin concluded.
The former director of the Federal penitentiary penitentiary service was put on trial
The Prosecutor’s office of Moscow approved the indictment on the criminal case investigated by GSU of the Investigative Committee about embezzlement of budget funds allocated for the Federal penitentiary service of Russia.
Before the court will be the former head of the prison Department Alexander Reimer and his deputy, who caused the FSIN damage in the amount of more than 2.7 billion rubles.
The Metropolitan Prosecutor’s office sent a criminal case to the Zamoskvoretsky district court against the former Director of the Federal Penitentiary Service of Russia Alexander Reimer, his former Deputy Nikolay Krivolapov, as well as the director of the Federal State Penitentiary Enterprise “Center for information and technical support and communication of the Federal Penitentiary Service” (FSUE TITS) Viktor Determinov.
Depending on the role and the degree of participation in the commission of crimes, they are accused of GSU of the Investigative Committee in Moscow under Part 3 of article 285 of the criminal Code of the Russian Federation (abuse of official powers, entailed grave consequences), part 4 of article 159 of the Criminal Code of the Russian Federation (fragency committed using their official position, as part of an organized group, on an especially large scale).
Krivolapov is also charged under Part 1 of Art. 222 of the Criminal Code of the Russian Federation (illegal acquisition and storage of ammunition).
According to the TFR, in 2010-2012 these persons fraudulically stole budget funds from the state treasury allocated by the Federal Penitentiary Service to provide the department with electronic monitoring of controlled persons, the so-called electronic bracelets.
To embezzle budget funds, the group members developed a scheme according to which the enterprise controlled by them FSUE CITOS, with which the relevant state contracts were concluded, carried out technical means of control and supervision, including “electronic bracelets”, and sold at prices overestimated several times.
Despite the fact of the fact that FSU CITOS did not have production equipment, buildings, structures for the placement of production facilities, allowing to create a completed cycle for the production of “electronic bracelets”, five state contracts worth more than 3.3 billion rubles have been concluded between the Federal Penitentiary Service of Russia.
AS a result of this scheme, more than 2 billion rubles turned out to be in the accounts of the Samara branch of FSUE, of which 1.2 billion rubles were stolen.
According to the investigation, more than 140 million rubles. cashed money was personally received by Mr. Reimer in his office from one of the accompanied accompaniments, a criminal case in respect of which is allocated to a separate proceeding.
Nikolay Krivolapov, who participated in the machinations, was found an unknown origin cartridge to the award pistol, which allowed him to induce an additional accusation.
in this case, the volume of which amounted to 133 volumes, FSIN filed a lawsuit for compensation of material damage in the amount of 2.7 billion rubles to the accused.
Player Hakan Schukyur is suspected of involvement in the coup.
The authorities of Turkey issued a warrant for the arrest of the former football player, and then member of Parliament Hakan Schukyur and conducted searches in the two houses of his family.
The star of the Turkish football of the 1990's - in the early 2000's, striker Hakan Shukur is wanted by the country's authorities in connection with an attempted coffENT hectare last month.
The foreward, who graduated from his sports career in 2008, is accused of belonging to an “armed terrorist group”.
We are talking about the Hizmet movement - a society associated with a well-known Turkish religious figure and oppositionist Fethullah Gülen.
It is his President Erdoğan who considers the organizer of the attempted military coup that took place on July 15.
Fethullah Gülen resides in U.S. and the Turkish authorities are demanding his extradition.
According to local media reports, an arrest warrant for Hakan Schukyur was issued today, the police have already conducted searches in two houses that belong to the family of the former football player.
According to the report of the investigation, the organization of Fethullah Gülen, in addition to Hakan Schukyur himself, his father was included.
However, there was neither the former football player or his relatives there was not there.
Now he and his family live in the United States.
On being a football player, Hakan Schukyur defended the colors of several Turkish clubs and played for the national national team.
He spent most of his career at Galatasaray.
In the list of foreign clubs there are Italian “Torino”, “Inter” and “Palermo”, as well as the English “Blackburn”.
However, in any of them he did not spend more than one season.
Hakan Schukyur still remains the most productive striker of the Turkish national national team: in his asset 112 matches for the national team and 51 goals scored.
In 2013, Hakan Schukyur resigned his deputy office due to a corruption investigation around Erdogan’s party and his inner entourage.
According to the Turkish newspaper Hurriyet, arrest warrants of at least 42 journalists were issued in Turkey on July 25.
They are accused of assisting a military upheaval and links with opposition Islamic preacher Fethullah Gülen, who lives in the U.S.
Taking into account the severity of the accusations, media employees can wait for prolonged prison terms - from ten years to a few life imprisonment.
Egor Konchalovsky wants to create a network of theaters only for domestic films.
“I would create a network of cinemas exclusively for Russian cinema, tickets for which cost 2-3 times less than for foreign-made films,” he said.
Mr. Konchalovsky notes that it is difficult for Russian films to compete for the viewer with large Hollywood films.
In our country, more than 100 films are made a year, of which an average of 20-25 films reach screens.
“And even it is very difficult for them to compete with “Transformers” and “Iron man”, in the promotion of which huge budgets have been pumped out”, – said the film director.
