The Russian Cosme-Med Company (RMK) is ready to take social responsibilities and pay more attention to the environmental aspects of its business.
This is corrobated, for example, because RIMC undertook to modernize one of the oldest and environmentally “dirty” enterprises of the country - Karabash measlavl plant.
Karabash mesmeling plant was founded by an English joint-stock company headed by Leslie Urkvart in 1910.
In Soviet times it was a significant industrial enterprise for the country's economy, and it actually ensured the vital activity of the whole city.
However, in the 1990-ies due to financial problems, the production was stopped, which entailed serious social problems in Karabash.
In 1998, it was decided to resubscend the work of the Karabash copper smelting plant.
It was also necessary to solve one of the main problems of the Karabash plant - an ecological plant.
By the beginning of the 2000-ies Karabash was already notorious as an environmental disaster zone.
The situation on Karabashmedi began to change in 2004, after the enterprise came under the management of the Russian Copper Company.
The company began to modernize the production, which began to gradually reduce the ecological burden on the environment.
This was recently noted by the Governor of the Chelyabinsk region Boris Dubrovsky, who visited in the first days of July “Karabashmed”.
The President of the Southern Urals called the changes that have taken place with the enterprise since Karabashmed moved to the RMK group.
The main measure to modernize "Krabashmedi" in recent years was the construction of a new sulfur-accipitated shop, which allows to capture up to 99.9% of metallurgical gases.
According to Vsevolod Levin, the president of the Russian Cosme-comfort, the volume of investments in this project amounted to about 7 billion rubles.
The next stage of the modernization of CJSC "Karabashmed" - the reconstruction of the converter redivision.
The replacement of three converters, custodilixes, and ga-and-river tract is planned at the end of 2017.
the cost of the project - 2.5 billion rubles.
In addition, at the end of 2016 it is planned to launch a new workshop for the treatment of industrial effluents worth 1 billion ruble.
In turn, the amount of taxes deducted to Karabash will also increase.
For the entire period for the period for the implementation of the Tominsky GOK project - from the beginning of construction and before the commissioning of the second queue, the federal treasury will receive 8.9 billion rubles.
And after the commissioning of GOK, the flow of taxes to the budgets of all levels may amount to 80.9 billion rubles.
For a year of production in the Varnensky district, 346.3 million rubles have been credited in the budgets of different levels.
And that's for the first year.
“The longer the enterprise works successfully, the amount of declarages can be greater,” added Valery Ulanovsky.
RMK specified that in 2015, tax deductions from Mikheyevsky GOK came close to 1 billion rubles.
However, the participation of RMK enterprises in the life and the development of the territories of their presence is not limited to tax declarations.
RMK enterprises help to renovate and maintain schools, kindergartens, sports facilities, to build cultural and entertainment facilities, to improve territories.
In 2016, one of the largest social projects of the Russian copper company in Karabash was a major overhaul, and, in fact, an almost complete reorganization of the N9 Kindergarten by 95 pupil.
Built in 1960, was in an emergency condition.
Also on the territory of RMK Arena will accommodate a landscape park with an artificial pond, underground and above-ground parking for 600 cars, cafés and sports shops.
RMK Arena will allow to hold spectacular professional sports events of the international level.
But the main task of this project is to make physical education and sports in comfortable conditions available to residents of Chelyabinsk, primarily for children.
