Employees of the Sandholm refugee centre in Denmark suspected that teenagers living in him were engaged in prostitution.
About it on Thursday, August 11, reports The Local.
According to him, some teenagers told the staff of the institution that “someone in Copenhagen will organize prostitution classes”.
As noted in the publication, doubts of employees of the shelter arose after the Swedish newspaper Sydsvenkan told about similar stories in Malma.
In 2015, a crisis erupted in the European Union due to an influenction of refugees from the countries of Africa and the Middle East.
Denmark has placed on its own territory more than 20 thousand of them.
A fisherwoman caught a rare blue lobster.
The man found crustaceans among others caught in his underwater trap, according to ABC News.
The American plans to transfer him to a local aquarium.
The lobster weighs about a kilogram.
Wayne Nickerson (Wayne Nickerson) is catching lobsters for the past 35 years.
According to his wife, for the first time in the career of a man came across a blue Omar in 1990.
According to ABC News, crustaceans acquire a blue or blue crèches as a result of genetic changes.
In April of 2016 it became known that the fishermen caught off the coast of Japan a speciman of the rare species of deep-sea shark Megachasma pellagios (large shark).
