The President of Russia Vladimir Putin expressed the hope that Anton Vyno as the new head of the administration of the head of state will contribute to its constructive work.
According to RIA Novosti, the corresponding statement of the Russian leader made at a meeting with Vaino and his predecessor - Sergey Ivanov.
The Russian leader noted that the candidacy of Vaino for the post of the head of the presidential administration was recommended by Ivanov himself.
Putin passured the latter for the work done.
On August 12, Putin withdrew Ivanov from the post of head of the administration of the head of the head of state.
Vino took this post in his steak in his place.
The authorities of the French city of Cannes forbade visiting local beaches in burqini - a special bathing suit for women, which completely covers the body from the head to the ancestor.
About it on Friday, August 12, reports ABC News.
The mayor of Cann David Lisnard (David Lisnard) explained that such clothing "does not meet the rules of decency, the principles of secularism and does not comply with standards of hygiene and safety."
Also, according to him, the clothes, which emphasize religious affiliation, can cause violations of public order.
For wearing burqini introduced a fine in the amount of 38 euros (approximately 42 dollars).
It is noted that the ban was introduced against the background of the terrorist attacks, which were carried out on July 15 in Nice and on July 26 in the church of the city of Saint-Etien du Rouvre in the north of the country.
After its introduction, several Muslim women appealed to the court, stating that the restrictions violated the right to freedom of religion.
Blagoveshchensk city court (Amur region) sentenced the former head of the city Alexander Miguly to nine years in a general-regime colony.
About it on Friday, August 12, is reported on the website of the court.
Miguly was found guilty of committing crimes under articles 286 (“Amboration of authority”), 285.1 (“Integral spending of budget funds”) and 285 (“Abuse of official powers”) of the Criminal Code of the Russian Federation.
The investigation established that the official in December 2008 provided his friend a land plot in the village of Mukhinka with a violation of the procedure established by land legislation.
In 2006, he illegally issued an order on the purchase of a roadbridge over the Chigiri river, at an inflated price without competitive procedures and the conclusion of a municipal contract, Interfax clarifies.
In addition, in the period from 2007 to 2010, Migula in the interests of a commercial organization controlled by him, changed the terms of payments under the contract of sale of the lease of a land plot, which was provided for the construction of housing, and also liberated the company from rent.
As a result, the regional budget lost more than 5 million rubles, and the city treasury is about 21 million rubles.
On August 4) it became known that the former mayor, who is detained on suspicion of Corruption, who claimed a deputy’s mandate, did not provide subscription lists to participate in elections to the state Duma on time in the electoral Commission and was removed from the pre-election race.
Migula was detained in May 2015 on the territory of the Lipetsk region and was placed in a pre-trial detention center.
Before that, since 2011, he has been on an international wanted list since 2011.
Aleksandr Migula served as mayor of Blagoveshchensk from November 2004 to April 2010.
In the Russian Ministry of foreign Affairs refuted the information about the releasing captured by the Taliban Russian helicopter.
Information about the negotiations on Friday, August 12, in an interview with “Interfax” was shared by the special representative of the President of the Russian Federation for Afghanistan, the Director of the Second Department of the Asian foreign Ministry Zamir Kabulov.
This information could not be confirmed.
“The crew is still in captivity, negotiations are underway,” Kabulov said.
On August 11, a source in diplomatic circles told the agency that the captivants had been liberated.
According to him, the former hostages were transferred to Pakistan.
On August 4, it was reported that a Pakistani Mi-17 helicopter flying from Peshawar had landed in Logar province in eastern Afghanistan due to technical problems.
The builders of the Crimean bridge acquired an an anthem "I'm scoring pile".
On the YouTube-channel project "Crimean bridge" there was a clique "I am scoring piles".
This is the song of the builder of this structure - the hero says that the bridge will help "not to lose communication with a huge country."
The author, in particular, sings about how he “scoring the piles”.
On the music put a video from the construction site of the Crimean bridge.
Konstantin Khomenko wrote the song - the designer from the "Institute Giprostroymost - St. Petersburg", who developed the construction project.
It is not a professional musician.
The interior of the Ministry of internal Affairs of Thailand was blamed for the explosions in the resorts of local saboteurs.
Explosions in the resorts of Thailand - "acts of local sabotage" and are not associated with the activities of international terrorists.
About it, according to Reuters reports, said the police of Thailand.
According to law enforcement officers, they have not yet been able to find out whether these blamshells are connected with each other.
According to the main version, their organizers tried to thwart the tourist season.
It is possible that behind the bangs there are Muslim separators from the south of the country.
Law Enforcement authorities have already detained several people.
At the present moment it is known about the four dead and several dozen wounded.
The Prime Minister of Prayut Chang Ocha ordered additional security measures to prevent new blamshells and exclude possible victims.
In the tourist resorts of Thailand on Friday, August 12, there was a series of explosions.
The devices worked near police stations on the island of Phuket, in the cities of Surat Thani (the capital of the eponymous province, on the territory of which the Samui island is located)
Another explosive device, planted on the beach, was defused by sappers.
In the afternoon, on August 1, two bangs occurred in the resort city of Huaukhin.
Bombells were located in pots from the plants and were activated using a call from a mobile phone.
Among the victims - 10 foreign tourists, there are no Russians among them.
The British jewelry house Graff has unveiled a new Clock model The Peacock Watch made in the form of a peacock feather
Circle is decorated with a scaffold of diamonds.
To do this, the jewelers used not only classical round stones, but also bugets, as well as trap-yieven diamonds of graduation and emerald cut.
This quartz-movie clock and blue rudders of the Characterized Graff design are created in a single specimen and are presented in a Mercury boutique at the Four Seasons Moscow hotel.
The publication does not name the price of them.
Graff is a jewelry and watch house, founded in 1960 in London by Lawrence Gruff.
Produces jewelry with precious stones, predominantly with rippled diamonds (including in color) and watch (since 2008).
Quarmotive holder of the British Royal Prize in the field of international commerce (1977, 1994, 2006, 2014).
In different years, Graff purchased extremely rare and valuable diamonds, in particular the pink Empress Rose, Star of America, The Sara and others.
JK Rowling’s new book, “Harry Potter and the Cursed Child”, became the best-selling in the U.K.
The novel overshadowed the popular play “Romeo and Juliet” by William Shacksiy.
According to the publication, for the first week after the release of the eighth part of the wizard saga, 847.9 thousand specimens were sold.
“Harry Potter and the Cursed Kidnant” brought £8.76.
At the same time, the tragedy of Shakespeare turned out to be in second place - since 1998, almost 127,7 thousand books by Penguin Classics have been sold.
The eighth part of the saga about the wizard wizard "Harry Potter and the cursed child" was published on July 3.
The action of the play unfolds 19 years after the events described in the book “Harry Potter and Dares of Death”.
On the same day in London on the stage of the theater Palace held the premiere of the play on the play.
In Russia, an English-language version of the romance entered the sheavals of the "Moskov House of Books" - the only official seller of the romance on August 5.
All specimens were sold out in a day.
In the Russian, a new part of the saga will be released before the end of 2016.
Owners of instant messengers and postal services should identify users and delete prohibited information - this is a brief summary of the bill, developed by the Media Communication Union (ISS), which unites the largest Russian communication operators (Vedomosti has it).
Employees of the three companies - members of the Union confirmed that such a project is being negotiated.
In the beginning of the autumn he should be presented to the working group under the leadership of first Deputy Prime Minister Igor Shuvalov, said the interlocutor of “Vedomosti” in the ISS.
We are talking about amendments to the laws on communication and on the media.
They stipulates that any “disseating information on the Internet, which provides the possibility of exchanging electronic messaging”, is obliged to identify users on the basis of the information contained in the databases of communication operators, having previously concluded contracts with them.
And “immediately to block messages or publications that contain information disseminated in violation of the requirements of Russian legislation”.
Otherwise, the operators have the right to restrict access to the service according to Roskomnadzor.
Astronomers have discovered a mysterious space object behind Neptune.
Astronomers have discovered a mysterious cosmic object behind Neptune.
Celestial body is very faint, its diameter is about 200 kilometers, writes the publication New Scientist.
According to the researchers, the object is moving along a completely uncharacteristic orbit for the solar system.
It is almost perpendicular relative to other planets.
The mysterious discovery was called Niku, which means “removable”, “unconquered” translated from Chinese.
WSJ: the United States is considering the imposition of sanctions against the Russian Federation due to the burglary of the servers of the Democrats.
US officials are considering the imposition of new sanctions against Russia in response to the hacking of the servers of the Democratic party, writes The Wall Street Journal, citing sources.
It is reported that for the imposition of sanctions, the administration of U.S. President Barack Obama will have to be officially accused of an attack on the servers of Russia or hackers supported by the Russian authorities.
According to the sources, the FBI and other American special services are almost convinced of Russia's involvement in a cyberattack.
