FAS has fined Google almost half a billion ruble
The reason was the influencing of competition in the mobile application market.
The antimonopoly proceedings were initiated by “Yandex”.
The Russian company claimed that Google provides smartphone builders with access to Android components on conditions that have prohibited pre-installation of applications from other developers, in Participating Yandex.
FAS found confirmation of these claims and established, the company abused a dominant position in the market and forced the manufacturers of mobile devices the installation along with the Google Play store of other applications.
According to the results of the audit, the Federal Antimonopoly service has decided to punish Google, said the Deputy head of the FAS Alexei Dotsenko.
The penalty must be paid within 60 days after the entry into force of the decree.
The FAS concluded that the law on the protection of competition must comply with all companies, including transnational corporations.
In turn, Google intend to first study the decision and will only then be determined with further actions: to perform it or to challenge.
The Federal antimonopoly service recognized the company as a violator of the law on competition in September last year and ordered to adjust the contracts until December.
However, Google didn’t agree.
Since then, the company and agencies have been conducting legal proceedings.
The FAS noted that, regardless of the penalty, they are discussing the possibility of concluding a emi-agreed agreement with Google.
This measure will not lead to anything.
This opinion "Echo of Moskvy" was expressed by the leading analyst of Mobile research group Eldar Murtazin.
Murtazin also noted that the penalty will not affect either the users or the competitiveness of the corporation.
