Blossus shows inflation for the first time in 8 months
Inflation in Bulgaria was 1% monthly in July, according to national statistics.
This is the highest figure for the years (from June 2012) and the first above zero since October last year, when positive 0.2% were shown.
Medieval-annorth inflation, measured by the CCI, over the past 12 months (August 2014-July 2015) was -0.8% compared to the previous 12 months (August 2014-July 2015).
The consumer price index in July of 2016 compared with June 2016 amounted to 101.0%, i.e. monthly inflation was 1.0%.
Inflation index since the beginning of the year (July 2016 in comparison with December 2015) accounted -0.2%, and the annual inflation in July 2016 compared to July 2015 was -0.2%.
In July of 2016, compared with the previous month, an increase was observed in prices for the following groups of consumer goods: food and non-alcoholic beverages (1..7%); transport (1.8%); recreation and culture (6.3%); restaurants and hotels (1.2%); other goods and services (0.3%).
Prices fell on clothing and footwear (2.2 per cent), furniture, household appliances and regular maintenance (0.5%); health (0.1%).
Prices remained at the same level in the previous month for alcoholic beverages and tobacco; living conditions, water, electricity, gas and other types of fuel; communication systems; and education.
