The representatives of the Democratic party in the Intelligence Committee of the U.S. House of Representatives published on Thursday their own data, which will be consistent with some of the conclusions of the republican task force.
“Between in 2014 and 2015, Centcom created an excessively closed procedure for the production of intelligence assessments for ISIL and Iraqi security forces,” House of Representatives member Adam B. Schiff said in a statement.
This procedure, according to Schiff, “stopped the issuance of reconnaissance documents”, caused damage to the moral condition of analysts and “insufficiently reflects divergent views”.
But Schiff and Democrats argue that they found no evidence that the White House was trying to forced Centcom analysts to fit their sentences under a “dedicated or politically interpreted.”
Preliminary results of the congressional investigation were presented on Tuesday portal The Daily Beast.
