The Jewish Director sharply criticized the Berlin hotel for the deletion of the phone code of the Israel on the “request” of the Arabs – said the channel RT News
The French director of Jewish origin unveiled the scandal in the media, discovering that Kempinski Bristol in Berlin does not have Israel’s telephone code list, and the employees refer to “receipts” from Arab customers.
Claude Lanzman, the author of the documentary about the Holocaust “Shoa”, expressed his dissatisfaction with Kempinski Bristol hotel in Berlin, writing an open letter to the German media FAZ.
During his recent stay at the Lantzmann Hotel, he tried to find Israel in the list of telephone codes provided by the hotel.
The country, however, was not mentioned among the states where you can call directly from the room.
How could it happen that in 2016 in Berlin, the capital of a new Germany, Israel was excluded and eradicated?
Wrote Lantzmann.
Instead, Kempinkski Bristol provides an opportunity to recruit Israel through its own telephone service center.
In the search for an explanation, the director picked up this issue at the reception of the hotel.
The answer that he received there, according to Lanzman, “shocked him.”
Clerk said that this measure was a "deliberate decision of the management of the Kempinkski hotel chain."
The reason behind this step aroused an even greater wretched by the director.
“Most of our guests are Arab, and they demanded that the Israeli code be removed,” Lantzmann, an employee of the hotel said.
The Israeli Ambassador to Germany Yakov Hadas-Khandelsman called the case a “terrible disgrace”, – according to the newspaper Suddeutsche Zeitung.
We were shocked and shocked by the incident.
It's actually a terrifying disgrace.
The fact that this happened in Germany and in this network of hotels is an even greater disgrace.
Expediation is not needed here.
We are expecting that the hotel will draw the right conclusions,” – said the official said.
The case caused considerable resonance on the Internet; people called it a scandal.
Some argued that the Kempinski hotel simply “came along” with the alleged demands of Arab customers.
“Assessed”, – said in another post, indicating that the hotel, located on the glorious Kurfurstendamm street, is located next to a synagogue.
The hotel hurried to dismiss any accusations, calling the incident a “unspectrum” and “apologizing” before Lanzman, the newspaper Der Spiegel said.
“There has never been any direct order not to include Israel in the fast dilihood list”, – quotes a representative of the hotel Quempinski newspaper Suddeutsche Zeitung.
She adds that the code has now been enclosed.
The police uses tear gas and retarded gulls against protesting Brazilian students
The students clashed with the police in the Brazilian city of São Paulo on Thursday, when gathered to protest against the government reforms of the public education system.
The police used tear gas and rubber bullets against the protesters.
Unrest began when police officers tried to dismantle the students, as a result of which the police used rubber bullets and tear gas.
Hundundreds of students took part in the demonstration to express their concerns about the plans.
In accordance with the proposals of the Governor of São-Paul, Geraldo Alckmin almost 100 public secondary schools will be closed, and 300 000 pupils will be redistributed in order to save money.
Some participants in the protests could be seen for writing graffiti on the walls, directed against interim President Michael Temer.
This last protest came just a few days after the protesters took to the streets encircled to support ousted President Dilma Rousseff, when the country's senate voted for her impeachment.
trade between Russia-Ir-Iran increased by 71% – according to the portal RT Business
With the repeal of sanctions, the trade turnover between Moscow and Tehran increased by 70.9 per cent compared with the previous year, according to Russia’s Ambassador to Iran Levan Dzhagaryan.
Since international sanctions against Iran were lifted, there is an increase in interest from Russian firms in doing business in the country, the ambassador said.
Russian companies are resuming ties with Iran, and new firms are ready to get access to the market.
Of course, the further expansion of trade is one of the main priorities of bilateral cooperation with Iran,” Dzhagaryan said.
He noted that for the first five months of 2016 the trade turnover between Russia and Iran increased by 70.9 percent compared with the same period in 2015 and amounted to $ 856 million.
In particular, the Russian exports to Iran grew by 91.5 percent and amounted to $ 697 million.
Russian imports from Iran increased by 16 percent, to 158 million dollars.
An increase in trade was achieved thanks to the supply of machinery, ground vehicles and weapons,” the ambassador said.
Dzhagaryan also predicts that this year Russia will be visited by a record number of Iranian tourists.
Last year the Russian diplomatic mission in Iran issued about 35 000 visas, mainly tourist, to citizens of Iran.
In addition, for the first time Iran entered the top 20 countries in terms of the number of tourists visiting Russia.
We can confidently say that last last year's record for the number of Iranian tourists who visited Russia will be beaten," he said.
At the same time, relatively a few Russians are visiting Iran, which the ambassador hopes will change.
“I personally recommend visiting the cities of Isfahan, Shiraz and Yazd, where monuments of the ancient Persian civilization are preserved in good condition,” he said.
The state continues to twist nuts in the military-industry complex.
The reason for dismantling was the “systematic non-implementation” of the instructions of the General Director of the concern “Almaz-Antey”, “losing in work” and “loss of trust”.
Gennady Bandera has been appointed the head of the NGO for the next three years.
Information about the dismissal of Neskordov appeared only on Thursday evening and did not cause a wide resonance in the media.
How to Explain Such Silence in the Conditions of Large-explosive Re-Armed Armament?
Most likely, the leadership of the Russian Federation does not want to spread any rumors or negative assumptions in the public.
This once again proves that there are a lot of problems among the military-industrial complex (PPC) and the state does not want to attract increased public attention to them.
Suspension of Neskordov is undoubtedly an important event from the point of view of restoring order in the industry.
NGO Almaz - the parent company of the concern, which specializes in the production of anti-aircraft-missile complexes (SAMs) of marine and land-based.
At the present, "Lymaz" is working on the creation of air defense systems "Polyment-Redut" and "Morfey", which are planned to be installed on new corvettes, frigates, destroyers and cruising.
The founder of the portal Military Russia Dmitry Kornev believes that the dismantling of Neskordov is caused by a breakdown of deadlines for these projects.
This version is the most logical.
For example, the development of "Morpheus" began back in 2007, and commissioning was expected in 2013.
"Polyment-Redute" should become the main air defense system on the latest ships of the Navy.
According to the information that I am receiving, for several years of the tests there was not a single truly successful test.
However, as far as I can judge, there is no unequivourable fault of the Almazar," Kornev said.
The expert fears that the delay with the commissioning can also occur with the S-500 air defense systems.
Experimental design work on the project has not yet been completed, but during 2016 the first complexes should come to the troops.
The Ministry of defense assures that “still work is being carried out and everything will be completed on time”, although in 2014 the Ministry recognized the presence of problems with the development of the S-500.
Extremely difficult to give an assessment of the professional qualities of Neskordov, who headed Almaz since 2011.
Kornev stated that the disruption of deadlines for the projects can be both an occasion and the reason for the dismissal.
In his opinion, in recent years it has become extremely difficult to obtain information about the internal processes in the defense industry and the plans for the management of enterprises.
The industry received long-term orders for tens of billions of ruble rubles, and a lot of money, as you know, loves silence.
As a rule, the directors of defense companies leave their positions at their own will, under an agreement agreement of the parties or are transferred to another job.
In this case, the suspension took place publicly, albeit did not receive resonance.
This puts the idea that the leader of “Diamond” was, perhaps, an obstinate figure, and resisted “disburners” lowered from above.
It seems that with such behavior, the state no longer intends to reconcile.
With the hands of the shareholders, it will disqualify those who prefer to argasy argue with the units of the Ministry of Defense and do not fulfill their tasks.
Simultaneously, the leadership of the Russian Federation strives to punish the stole managers (fragments at the Zvezda shipyard).
Increased attention to the problems of the sector is paid personally by the president.
Volodymyvil Putin heads the Military-Industrial Commission and periodically holds meetings on re-equilibrium.
The Kremlin protects the ranks of the defense industry managers, aiming to have at the fingerhiding a loyal composition of directors, who will carry out orders received on top.
